  title: Bindusara
  text: Bindusara, son of Chandragupta, ruled from about 297 to 273 BCE and extended the empire into the Deccan. Greek sources call him Amitrochates, slayer of foes. He kept diplomatic ties with the Seleucid kingdom of Syria.
